        "job": "Say whether a package's manifest names only permissions the host has a row for, and what each permission it names lets it do",
        "description": "Give manifest ({ permissions: [ids] }) and, if wanted, permissions (the host's own rows, each { id, says, calls }; the shipped rows otherwise: network_egress, read_files, write_files, run_programs, use_microphone, read_screen). A permission with no row is refused, never ignored. Answers ok, unknown (the ids with no row), needs (the rows of the ids it named) and why when one is unknown.",
